## Acceptance contract

Todo 24 requires an already-live two-host stream, forcible client-process termination without
sending Stop, a timestamped last-heartbeat observation, and a timestamped Linux transition to
Idle/capture stop between 30 and 35 seconds inclusive. It then requires a fresh session to stream
normally and requires the server process to survive the whole scenario. The tray Exit path was not
used.

## Server state-machine preflight

The required codegraph inspection was completed before host activity. The current control-plane
contract is:

- `HEARTBEAT_TIMEOUT = Duration::from_secs(30)` in `apps/wifimic_server/src/control.rs`.
- The server lifecycle states are `Idle`, `Starting`, and `Streaming`.
- The Todo 6 deterministic timeout test already records the intended transition as
  `Streaming -> Idle`, one capture stop, and `HeartbeatTimeout`; that unit evidence is not a
  substitute for this real-host acceptance run.
- The production loop polls the UDP socket with a bounded read timeout so `ControlPlane::advance`
  can enforce the liveness deadline without a separate timer thread (recorded in the notepad
  decisions).

